HESS UPDATE V3

AI Implementation & Repository Execution Protocol

Document Type: AI Agent Operating Instructions
Status: Authoritative workflow for the V3 implementation agent
Project Model: New repository / independent rebuild
Old Hess Repository: Reference only


---

1. Mission

You are responsible for building Hess V3 as a new project and new repository.

This is not a migration of the existing Hess application.

The existing Hess repository is available only as a reference implementation and source of historical evidence.

Your goal is to understand what Hess is, understand what the previous implementation attempted, understand what failed, and then build a new, clean implementation according to the V3 specifications.

The intended result is:

A correct Hess engine → reliable AI → secure multiplayer → polished Hess experience → useful learning system.

Do not optimize for speed at the expense of understanding or verification.


---

2. The Three Roles of the Project Material

There are three different categories of information you will encounter.

A. V3 Documents — Authority

These define what the new Hess V3 should be.

B. Old Hess Repository — Reference

This explains how Hess was previously implemented.

It is useful evidence, but it is not authoritative.

C. Historical Game Logs / Existing Behavior — Evidence

These can reveal:

bugs

edge cases

unexpected interactions

AI weaknesses

usability problems

interesting gameplay situations


They do not automatically define the rules.


